    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "dee9bc9e_f9a3cd2d",
        "filename": "core/cortex-m/atomic.h",
        "patchSetId": 2
      },
      "lineNbr": 76,
      "author": {
        "id": 1256783
      },
      "writtenOn": "2018-09-21T03:00:03Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "At the moment the logic to do reset is spread across at least two tasks, so I\u0027m not sure it\u0027s possible to do the whole reset with interrupts disabled.\n\nIf portability is an issue (though I am guessing this operation wouldn\u0027t be hard to re-implement on other architectures - it is very similar to the other atomic operations) then it should be possible to make a small tweak to the design so that we just have the same state variable as now and protect it with a standard mutex rather than using these operations, which could then be removed.\n\nI guess I went with this (other than because it was kinda fun ;) because it\u0027s faster and requires less code and less RAM.",
      "parentUuid": "3c5c9198_e910b7ef",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 76,
        "startChar": 2,
        "endLine": 76,
        "endChar": 33
      },
